    {
      "text": "Introduction to Left-Right Symmetric Models — We motivate left-right symmetric models by the possibility of spontaneous parity breaking.\n\n**Introduction to Left-Right Symmetric Models**\n\n13 pp, 12 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We motivate left-right symmetric models by the possibility of spontaneous parity breaking. Th,;n we describe the multiplets and the La.grangian of such models. Finally we discuss lower bounds on the right-handed scale. *) Lectc:re given at.the 4th Hellenic School on Elementary Particle Physics, Corfu, 2- 20 September 1992.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; Abstract; 1 Motivation and Basic Ingredients; Motivation For LR-Symmetric Models:; 2.1 Basic Multiplets and Interactions; WfR(x); 3 Spontaneous Symmetry Breaking; (AL,R)o = yl2; 4.2 Quark Mixing; 5 Lepton Sector; Acknowledgement; References",
      "lang": "en",
